  "text": "We are given two sequences:\n\n- The **Fibonacci sequence** $ F(n) $ defined by:\n  $$\n  F(n) = F(n-1) + F(n-2), \\quad \\text{with } F(1) = F(2) = 1\n  $$\n\n- A **second sequence** $ (a_n) $ defined by:\n  $$\n  a_n = 3a_{n-1} - 2a_{n-2}, \\quad \\text{with } a_1, a_2 \\in \\mathbb{Z}^+\n  $$\n\nWe are to **find all pairs** $ (a_1, a_2) $ such that the **number of positive terms less than 2000** is the **same** for both sequences.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Understand the Fibonacci sequence\n\nWe can compute the Fibonacci numbers up to the first one that is **greater than or equal to 2000**.\n\nLet’s compute the Fibonacci sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{align*}\nF(1) &= 1 \\\\\nF(2) &= 1 \\\\\nF(3) &= 2 \\\\\nF(4) &= 3 \\\\\nF(5) &= 5 \\\\\nF(6) &= 8 \\\\\nF(7) &= 13 \\\\\nF(8) &= 21 \\\\\nF(9) &= 34 \\\\\nF(10) &= 55 \\\\\nF(11) &= 89 \\\\\nF(12) &= 144 \\\\\nF(13) &= 233 \\\\\nF(14) &= 377 \\\\\nF(15) &= 610 \\\\\nF(16) &= 987 \\\\\nF(17) &= 1597 \\\\\nF(18) &= 2584 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n$$\n\nSo, the **number of Fibonacci numbers less than 2000** is:\n\n- $ F(1) $ to $ F(17) $: 17 terms\n- $ F(18) = 2584 > 2000 $\n\nSo, **17 Fibonacci numbers less than 2000**.\n\nWe will **later** count how many **positive terms** of the sequence $ (a_n) $ are **less than 2000**, and we want this count to be **17**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Understand the recurrence relation of $ a_n $\n\nGiven:\n$$\na_n = 3a_{n-1} - 2a_{n-2}, \\quad a_1, a_2 \\in \\mathbb{Z}^+\n$$\n\nThis is a **linear recurrence relation** with constant coefficients. Let’s find its **general solution**.\n\n#### Step 2.1: Characteristic equation\n\nThe characteristic equation of the recurrence is:\n\n$$\nr^2 - 3r + 2 = 0\n$$\n\nSolving:\n\n$$\nr = \\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{9 - 8}}{2} = \\frac{3 \\pm 1}{2} = 2, 1\n$$\n\nSo the general solution is:\n\n$$\na_n = A \\cdot 2^n + B \\cdot 1^n = A \\cdot 2^n + B\n$$\n\n#### Step 2.2: Apply initial conditions\n\nLet’s use the initial conditions $ a_1 = A \\cdot 2 + B $, and $ a_2 = A \\cdot 4 + B $.\n\nLet’s denote:\n\n$$\na_1 = 2A + B \\\\\na_2 = 4A + B\n$$\n\nSubtract the two:\n\n$$\na_2 - a_1 = 2A \\Rightarrow A = \\frac{a_2 - a_1}{2}\n$$\n\nThen:\n\n$$\nB = a_1 - 2A = a_1 - 2 \\cdot \\frac{a_2 - a_1}{2} = a_1 - (a_2 - a_1) = 2a_1 - a_2\n$$\n\nSo the general term is:\n\n$$\na_n = A \\cdot 2^n + B = \\left( \\frac{a_2 - a_1}{2} \\right) \\cdot 2^n + (2a_1 - a_2)\n$$\n\nSimplify:\n\n$$\na_n = (a_2 - a_1) \\cdot 2^{n-1} + 2a_1 - a_2\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Count the number of positive terms of $ a_n $ less than 2000\n\nWe need to find for which **initial values** $ (a_1, a_2) $, the number of **positive terms** $ a_n < 2000 $ is **17** (",
